    "scenario": "MPLS L3VPN over a GRE Core",
    "goals": "• {{router1_name}} and {{router4_name}} are the two provider edge routers of a layer 3 VPN. {{router2_name}} and {{router3_name}} in between belong to a plain IP transit network that does not run MPLS and must not start running it.\n    OSPF process 1 area 0 already runs on all three physical links and carries only the Loopback0 addresses, so {{router1_loopback0_ip}} and {{router4_loopback0_ip}} already reach each other over the transit.\n• Each PE already holds the VPN routing instance {{vrf_name}} with route distinguisher {{rd}} and route target {{rt}}, a customer network on Loopback1 inside it ({{router1_loopback1_cidr}} and {{router4_loopback1_cidr}}), a second loopback used as the MPLS and BGP endpoint ({{router1_loopback2_ip}} and {{router4_loopback2_ip}}), and a VPNv4 session in AS {{as_number}} configured between those two endpoint addresses. That session cannot come up yet.\n• Build a GRE tunnel Tunnel{{tunnel_id}} between the two PEs, sourced from Loopback0 and destined to the remote Loopback0, addressed out of {{tunnel_cidr}} ({{tunnel_ip1}} on {{router1_name}}, {{tunnel_ip2}} on {{router4_name}}).\n• Advertise the endpoint loopbacks to each other through the tunnel only: run a second OSPF process {{overlay_process}} in area 0 that covers the tunnel subnet and the local Loopback2 host route. Do not put Loopback2 into OSPF process 1, otherwise the endpoint would be reachable over the physical path and the VPN traffic would leave the tunnel.\n• Enable MPLS forwarding with LDP on the tunnel and take the LDP router-id from Loopback2, so the two PEs build an LDP session between {{router1_loopback2_ip}} and {{router4_loopback2_ip}} and a label switched path across the GRE core.\n• Result: the LDP session and the VPNv4 session must both be up between the endpoint loopbacks, both customer prefixes must appear in the VPNv4 table, the two customer loopbacks must be able to ping each other inside {{vrf_name}}, and {{router2_name}} and {{router3_name}} must have no MPLS configuration at all.",
